    AND premises's `at the address in the Policy Summary`

§§ `The Insured's Family`

-- Spouse, children and relatives of the Insured who regularly live with the Insured at the
-- Insured Location. F-family: "regularly live with" governs all three (reading (i), taken);
-- reading (ii) lets it govern "relatives" only. Part 2 limb (b) has to add "whether or not
-- living with the Insured" to reach a relative who does not, which is evidence for (i).
