GIVEN relation      IS A `A relation`
      `lives there` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a relative is in the Insured's Family, being` relation `, living with the Insured` `lives there` MEANS
    `lives there`

-- Reading (ii) of F-family, kept so the fork can be shown; no rule uses it.
@ref F-family, reading (ii), not taken
GIVEN relation      IS A `A relation`
      `lives there` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`on reading (ii), a relative is in the Insured's Family, being` relation `, living with the Insured` `lives there` MEANS
        relation EQUALS `a spouse`
    OR  relation EQUALS `a child`
    OR  `lives there`

§§ `Home (the building)`

-- A house or an apartment in an apartment building at the Insured Location, owned by the
-- Insured or for whose management and care the Insured is legally responsible, used wholly or
-- mainly as the Insured's private residence (part may be an office if approved).
